{
  // CONTRACT GATE: compiles the protocol surface with the Node type surface switched off, which turns
  // AGENTS.md section 4 ("contract and protocol code stays free of Node-only APIs") from a review
  // convention into a build failure.
  //
  // Why these three files and not more — this boundary was measured, not assumed:
  //
  //   - `src/lib/errors.ts` and `src/lib/mcp-tools.ts` are pure protocol: error codes and shapes, and the tool
  //     schemas. They must never need a process, a socket or a buffer.
  //   - `src/lib/mcp-protocol.ts` holds the JSON-RPC error mapping and the protocol/server identity
  //     constants. It was EXTRACTED from `src/lib/gateway.ts` for exactly this reason: that file is the
  //     stdio TRANSPORT and genuinely needs stdin/stdout, a pid and signal handlers, so nothing defined
  //     in it could be gated. Leaving the constants and the mapping in the transport would have made
  //     this gate either vacuous or a lie.
  //
  // `src/lib/gateway.ts` is deliberately NOT included: needing streams is legitimate for a transport, and
  // claiming otherwise would force a false abstraction. The checked property is that every wire shape,
  // error code and protocol constant is Node-free. `src/lib/ipc.ts` is excluded for the same reason — it is
  // the local socket transport — and the transport modules are checked by `tsconfig.json`.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2023"],
    "types": []
  },
  "include": [
    "src/lib/errors.ts",
    "src/lib/mcp-tools.ts",
    "src/lib/mcp-protocol.ts"
  ]
}
